  "details": "I'm requesting this on behalf of people I know who get tons of random friend requests over their avatars, and I was surprised there is no method of filtering who can send friend requests like you can in other platforms (IE: Discord), so I've made a mockup for what that could look like.\n\nI made these options in like 3 minutes, so they're not perfect, but my idea was:\n\n- Everyone\n\n- Friends of Friends\n\n- Group Members\n\n- Friends and Group\n\n- Nearby Users \n\n- Disabled\n\n\"Friends and Group\" is named that way because the text box is short\n\nNearby Users enforces the wants of those people who put \"don't friend request me unless we're in the same world together\" in their bios.\n\nI'd say the Friend Request error message would say something like \"You cannot friend request this person: Requests set to Disabled.\"",
